{%- comment -%}
  Outputs a product's stock state and the stock to show for it, separated by a space:
  "in_stock 12", "backorder 0" or "out_of_stock 0". Capture it and split on the space.

  The state comes from the Single (non-Case) variants only. Case variants hold no stock of their own
  and always continue selling, so a Case at 0 stock never makes a product "backorder"; cases are
  filled from the Single's stock (see blocks/_pdp-box-quantity.liquid).
  - in_stock: a Single has stock, or Shopify doesn't track its inventory
  - backorder: no Single has stock, but one is set to continue selling when out of stock
  - out_of_stock: no Single has stock and none can be oversold, so it can't be added to the cart

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} the product
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign stock_state = 'out_of_stock'
  assign stock_qty = 0
  for variant in product.variants
    if variant.option1 == 'Case' and product.variants.size > 1
      continue
    endif
    if variant.inventory_management != 'shopify' or variant.inventory_quantity > 0
      assign stock_state = 'in_stock'
      assign stock_qty = variant.inventory_quantity | at_least: 0
      break
    elsif variant.inventory_policy == 'continue'
      assign stock_state = 'backorder'
    endif
  endfor
  echo stock_state | append: ' ' | append: stock_qty
-%}
